<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phoebidas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 382 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phoebidas was a Spartan commander who in 382 BCE, while leading troops north against Olynthus, seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadmea">Cadmea</a>, the citadel of Thebes, with the help of a pro-Spartan Theban faction. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> fined him but kept the garrison, an act widely condemned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Theban exiles freed the city in 379 BCE, and Phoebidas was later killed in a skirmish near Thespiae while commanding the Spartan garrison there.</p></div>
